   "id": "6eb4cd853082",
   "metadata": {
    "evaluation_report": true
   },
   "source": [
    "### 7.7 Local explainability of the selected MLP\n",
    "\n",
    "We analysed all 166 true transition windows from nine test participants. The fixed eleven-window MLP refit matches all 3,162 labels saved in §6 of [MLP external.ipynb](companion/MLP%20external.ipynb) after posture memory. The base network classifies 152 of the 166 transition windows correctly. Memory raises this to 158.\n",
    "\n",
    "Occlusion and Integrated Gradients use the base network margin $m(x)=s_a(x)-s_b(x)$, where $a$ is the original top prediction and $b$ is the runner-up for correct predictions or the true class for errors. A positive margin drop means that replacing the input reduced support for $a$ relative to $b$. Row IDs are zero-based CSV positions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4d1bde65420e",
   "metadata": {
    "evaluation_report": true
   },
   "source": [
    "#### 7.7.1 Grouped window occlusion\n",
    "\n",
    "**Figure 11. Single-window occlusion.** Replace the 561 features at one time offset with the matching block from the training mean or a representative context for sitting, standing or lying. Each posture reference is the real training context nearest its class mean."
   ]
  },
