    "#### 7.7.2 Integrated Gradients and feature ablation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Table 31. Numerical accuracy and window agreement.** [Integrated Gradients](https://proceedings.mlr.press/v70/sundararajan17a.html) integrates the margin gradient along a straight path from a reference to the case. Feature attributions sum to the margin difference up to integration error. We used 64 trapezoidal intervals and refined difficult paths to 256. Median per-case Spearman correlations between signed window sums and occlusion effects range from 0.921 to 0.964 with the current window excluded."
   ]
