   "source": [
    "#### 7.7.3 Exploratory LIME-style surrogates\n",
    "\n",
    "**Table 34. Held-out local probability fits.** We used [LIME-style](https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.04938) sparse linear surrogates for ten base MLP class probabilities from eight windows of one test participant. We interpolate towards nearby training contexts and compare a control that shuffles each feature's displacements. The 13/4/4 training-participant pools supply separate fit, validation and audit donors. Validation chooses the sparse fit before audit. The anchor accounts for 5% of fitting weight.\n",
    "\n",
    "The criteria are audit weighted $R^2 \\ge 0.8$, MAE $\\le 0.05$, probability SD $\\ge 0.02$, anchor error $\\le 0.05$, and at most 20 terms. **Zero of ten** selected sparse fits pass. The highest audit $R^2$ is **0.7995**. We also show the row 51 fit selected under a 50-term cap."
   ]
  },
